    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\nThe change: the create audit line in `SaveOwner.service` now also logs `membershipLevel` and `membershipNumber`, while keeping the existing `id`, `customerCode`, and `registrationDate` fields.\n\nI reused the existing derivation logic rather than duplicating it \u2014 `MembershipNumber.of(...)`, `MembershipPoints.of(...)` fed into `MembershipLevel.of(...)`, and `HouseholdTier.isGold(owner, ownerRepository)` (the repository was already a parameter of the method). These are the same functions the `OwnerMapper`/`MembershipDecorator` use to populate the DTO, so the audit values match what the API returns.\n\nStructural impact stayed minimal: one file touched, one method changed (`SaveOwner.service`), which is `SaveOwner`'s only method (WMC_other = 0) and remains cyclomatic-complexity 1 \u2014 all added lines are straight-line calls, no branches.",
